{"file_path":"generate_docs.py","old_string":"block(red,'C-8','CRITICAL','Sections 8.4 and new 8.5 — Mexico data privacy and IMMEX','Each Party shall comply only with applicable United States privacy laws. Schedule E merely states that the Parties will include “appropriate provisions” for IMMEX.','Each Party shall comply with all applicable data-protection laws, expressly including Mexico’s Federal Law on Protection of Personal Data Held by Private Parties (LFPDPPP) and its Regulations. For Monterrey employee data, Trident is the controller and Polaris is the processor. The Parties shall implement or attach a data-processing addendum covering purpose limitation, documented instructions, privacy notices (avisos de privacidad), required consents or other lawful transfer mechanisms, security, subprocessors, breach notice to Trident within 48 hours after awareness, data-subject assistance, return/deletion and lawful retention. Trident is responsible for controller notices, lawful basis and employee-facing disclosures; Polaris shall process only for the Services.

